{"event": "decision_completed", "analyzer_name": "CSA (Clang Static Analyzer)", "iteration": 1, "action": "apply_patch", "summary": "Model the ownership relation precisely: a release mark is reportable only for the straight-line post-release use window; when a store re-acquires an already-released pointer value (or rebinds a variable carrying a stale released alias mark), the identical load result is a stale artifact of unmodeled container mutation after the release, so the checker drops the released state instead of propagating it — this kills the fixed-side loop-re-entry false positives (kfree/list re-derivation in the freeing loop) while preserving the vulnerable straight-line read of subflow->request_join after mptcp_close_ssk, which has no intervening re-acquisition.", "timestamp": 1790327397.86928}
